## Next existing dependency

The AWS-account and exact checkpoint-metadata blockers are resolved for this
observation. Do not repeat this acquisition or search for a fictitious tokenizer
checksum file. **The next software task is the resource-bounded real-4B CPU
restore/import successor**, integrating these verified metadata semantics with
closed inventory, tensor/dtype/tied-weight/HF-reload checks and an exact private
output budget. This task still needs real-sized resource planning; copying the
synthetic importer and raising its caps is not completion.

The full historical checkpoint is about 48.84 GB; the model-only portion is about
16.82 GB. Those inventory sizes do not authorize a partial restore or a large
download to the Mac. Dedicated host/geometry, source-compatible GPU worker,
actual import and data-relocation receipts, CUDA criteria and bounded execution
approval remain downstream. No GPU is required for this completed metadata task;
do not start GPU billing yet. Gate 5, real SFT and production eligibility remain
incomplete/false.
